          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph>From a small open source project in 1999 to Exponential 6.0.15: a quarter century of content management.</paragraph>
          </section>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="476" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph>Exponential has a long history. It began as eZ Publish, an open source content management system first released in 1999. eZ Publish was used by thousands of organizations and grew a large community; its commercial development was discontinued years ago.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>The community kept the code alive. Under the name Exponential it was brought to modern PHP, given new designs, new security features and a new application server, and released as 6.0.</paragraph>
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>Milestones</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>1999</strong>: the first open source release.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>2000s</strong>: content classes, the template language and ezflow landing pages.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>2020s</strong>: Exponential 6.0 on PHP 8, Velocity, expwt and site packages.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
